        "original_id": "9428f96d-c486-5d94-97c3-1002fbefff03",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Norman Z. McLeod, Sam Wanamaker, Wallace Beery, Marjorie Main\n- Roles: film director, cartoonist, writer, actor\n- Products: Jackass Mail\n- Topics: Hollywood blacklist, liberal sympathies\n\nFacts:\n- Norman Zenos McLeod was born on September 20, 1898, and he was an American film director, cartoonist, and writer.\n- Sam Wanamaker was born as Samuel Wattenmacker on June 14, 1919, and he was an American actor and director.\n- In 1942, Jackass Mail was released as a Western comedy film directed by Norman Z. McLeod and starring Wallace Beery and Marjorie Main.\n- Sam Wanamaker moved to the United Kingdom because he feared being blacklisted in Hollywood due to his early pronounced liberal sympathies.\n- Norman Z. McLeod died on January 27, 1964.\n- Sam Wanamaker, CBE, died on December 18, 1993.",
